  "description": "ASP.NET Core Identity stores persisted through Unified.Data.Tables' IStorage<T>: seven Entity-derived row models (one table each), deterministic key composition, and IUserStore/IRoleStore implementations covering passwords, external logins, claims, roles, tokens, 2FA and lockout. Depends only on the abstractions, so it runs against Azure Table Storage, the in-memory provider, or any other IStorage<T> — your whole Identity stack is unit-testable with no emulator.",
